      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cloud-sealed-memory-projection",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "The hosted memory projection stores a sealed snapshot under a grant that names a sealing scope (#1045 S4). AgentMemoryProjectionAuthorization's authorized result carries the grant's optional sealing { scopeId, epoch } (AgentMemoryProjectionSealing), and InMemoryAgentMemoryProjectionAuthorizer.grant takes it. The cloud refuses a snapshot whose form does not match its grant with 409 agent_memory_projection_sealing_mismatch. AgentMemoryProjectionCommitInput is a union: a plaintext mutation with its decoded redactedBytes, or a sealed mutation with none, which the store keeps as received and meters by padded length; a Host that implements its own AgentMemoryProjectionStore handles both. Postgres migration 0037 adds the sealed member to the head and contentMac and padded length to the receipt, with one-form checks, and rewrites no data.",
      "migration": "docs/migrations/1045-e2ee-v2.md#custom-projection-stores",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#AgentMemoryProjectionAuthorization",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#AgentMemoryProjectionCommitInput",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#AgentMemoryProjectionSealing",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#InMemoryAgentMemoryProjectionAuthorizer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cloud-sealed-agent-message",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "The cloud admits the sealed Agent message of a task whose sealing names agent-message, and advertises sealed-payload-v2 (#1045 S3). ByokCloudOptions.agentMessage is an AgentMessageConsumers: consume takes a plaintext message and consumeSealed a sealed one, which only a member can open; both are optional. A submission that seals agent-message with messageEgress is refused with agent_message_sealed_consumer_missing while consumeSealed is absent. TaskAgentMessage.payload and readAgentMessageDisposition return either form, as in 0.32.0; a sealed disposition names the message by contentMac. handleInboundEnvelope takes the AgentMessageConsumers object in place of the consume function.",
      "migration": "docs/migrations/1045-e2ee-v2.md#sealed-agent-messages",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#AgentMessageConsumeInput",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#AgentMessageConsumers",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#AgentMessageDecision",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#ByokCloudOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#handleInboundEnvelope"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "agent-memory-projection-grant-sealing",
      "impact": "additive",
      "summary": "AgentMemoryProjectionGrant takes an optional sealing { scopeId, epoch } (#1045 S2). With it, the daemon seals each memory projection snapshot under that Agent scope and never sends it in plaintext; without a usable key it sends nothing. The sealing is fixed for its writer epoch and survives a drained outbox: a grant at the same writer epoch with another sealing, plaintext included, fails with AgentMemoryError and sends nothing. An outbox written by 0.32.0 is bound plaintext, so sealing an existing Agent's projection takes a higher writer epoch. A Host that issues no sealing sees no change. The daemon also seals the Agent messages and memory evidence of a task whose offer names agent-message or memory-projection, and advertises sealed-payload-v2 whenever it advertises sealed-payload-v1.",
      "migration": "docs/migrations/1045-e2ee-v2.md#sealed-memory-projections",
      "items": [
        "config:agentMemory",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#AgentMemoryProjectionGrant"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "wire-v5-durable-lane",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "0.32.0 is the last v4 release. The envelope wire is v5 (PROTOCOL_VERSION = 5). The runtime capability durablePi is renamed durableLane (the durable worker lane, Pi today) in RuntimeCapabilitiesSchema, so on conn.hello runtimes and harnesses, task.claim, presence and PresenceRuntimeCapabilities; nothing else on the wire changes. There is no v4 reader and no negotiation: drain the v4 deployment (pending mailbox rows acknowledged, executions terminal, daemon pending terminals acknowledged), then start the server side and the daemons together. A pending v4 row stops startup with SQLITE_MAILBOX_PROTOCOL_UNSUPPORTED, POSTGRES_MAILBOX_PROTOCOL_UNSUPPORTED or DaemonJournalProtocolUnsupportedError and is left unchanged; retained rows open, so the stores need not be new. A hosted terminal receipt written by a v4 build no longer decodes (terminal_receipt_unreadable), so read the results you still need before the cut.",
      "migration": "docs/migrations/wire-v5-durable-lane.md#drain-and-upgrade",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/core#PresenceRuntimeCapabilities",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#ConnHelloPayloadSchema",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#HarnessInfoSchema",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#HarnessInventorySchema",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#MessagesSendRequestSchema",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#PROTOCOL_VERSION",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#PresencePublishRequestSchema",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#RuntimeCapabilitiesSchema",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#RuntimeInfoSchema",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#TaskClaimPayloadSchema",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol/constants#PROTOCOL_VERSION"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "runtime-generic-names",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "Runtime names are generic. DaemonConfig.durablePi is removed and raises DaemonConfigFieldRemovedError: set runtimes.pi.durableLane. PiAdapterOptions.durablePi and RuntimeCapabilities.durablePi are durableLane. The daemon wires the durable journal and durableContext from an adapter's capabilities.durableLane, so a Host that builds PiAdapter({ durableLane: true }) for createDaemonWithAdapters needs no daemon option, and such an adapter without an Agent home refuses to start. The launch resources are the new RuntimeLaunchResources (scratch, release()): RuntimeOperationStartInput.runtimeLaunch and PreparedRuntimeOperation.resolveRuntimeLaunch use it instead of the Pi type, which extends it.",
      "migration": "docs/migrations/wire-v5-durable-lane.md#runtime-names",
      "items": [
        "config:durablePi",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#PiAdapterOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#PreparedRuntimeOperation",
